  "title": "ASIN, ACOS, ATAN and ATAN2 of negative arguments, of the ends of the domain and in every quadrant",
  "matrix": ["functions.trigonometric-logarithmic-exponential"],
  "tags": ["arch-sensitive", "float"],
  "note": "ASIN and ACOS are defined on -1.0 to 1.0 (ASIN(-1.0) = -pi/2, ACOS(-1.0) = pi) and are not a number outside it; ATAN of a very large value approaches pi/2; ATAN2(Y, X) is the angle of the point (X, Y) in (-pi, pi]: ATAN2(1.0, -1.0) = 3*pi/4, ATAN2(-1.0, -1.0) = -3*pi/4, ATAN2(-1.0, 1.0) = -pi/4, ATAN2(1.0, 0.0) = pi/2 and ATAN2(0.0, 0.0) = 0",
